title: "agent-control-plane-casebook"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/agent-control-plane-casebook"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/agent-control-plane-casebook"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible failure cases from the control plane of a production multi-agent
  fleet: schedulers, registries, dispatchers and watchdogs that decide when and
  whether agents run. Each case carries a symptom, a plainly stated root cause, a
  stdlib-only deterministic repro of the mechanism, a detection guard shown red on
  the broken behavior, mitigation with residual risk, and dated evidence with
  upstream links. A casebook, not a benchmark: no scoring, no vendor comparisons.
  Independent, not affiliated with or endorsed by any vendor.
